      "text": "**What the exchange left behind.** After the early trades Black has four queenside pawns against White's three, but two are doubled (two pawns on one file), so that edge is not healthy. White has four kingside pawns against three, all undoubled. Black keeps both bishops. Whether the pawns outweigh the bishops is the question of the game; *a rule of thumb* says pawn structure matters more as pieces leave the board."
